      children: "Every AI application that does more than chat eventually runs into the same wall: the model is smart, but it is blind. It cannot see your database, cannot read your ticket tracker, cannot call your internal billing API, and cannot check the status of a deployment. For the model to be useful in a real business context, someone has to wire it up to the outside world, and until recently that wiring was bespoke, brittle, and repeated by every team that tried it. The Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is Anthropic's answer to that wiring problem. It is an open specification, not a product, and it has grown from a November 2024 release into what is now widely treated as the default way to connect large language model applications to tools, data, and services."
